acceptance_criteria: "Default-sort metadata preserves compatible legacy sort/order fields and exposes an ordered effective-key contract including registry-derived nonterminal-before-terminal grouping, priority ascending, updated_at descending and final ID ascending; Unfiltered lists disclose every comparator stage and the synthetic terminal grouping semantics explicitly; Brief projection includes priority when the effective sort uses it and updates projection.fields and omission receipts accurately; Explicit fields compact and full selections remain authoritative and explicit-sort behavior stays covered; Public SDK CLI MCP and TOON/JSON share the effective policy with configured defaults and stable tie breaking; Focused and packed controls preserve bounded continuation"
parent: pm-srns
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: "Agents can understand default list ranking from one bounded read, while explicit field selection and existing sorting/continuation compatibility remain intact."
