  "2026-10-20T06:57:02.960Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: preserve legacy sort/order metadata, disclose every effective comparator stage including registry-based terminal grouping, include priority in effective-default brief rows, and retain authoritative custom projections, explicit sorts and continuation semantics. Grouped with pm-65srr0 in one reviewed SDK context PR. Full live metadata and raw history read; prior pm-gh1481 and pm-6pycus remain completed narrower contracts."
  "2026-10-20T07:10:15.579Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: the pre-fix comparator keeper failed on missing effective_keys. Current focused cohort82/82 passes with exact four-stage metadata and brief priorities; new native/CLI JSON/TOON continuation acceptance is included in full coverage. The SDK snapshot explicitly classifies the optional metadata signature change while retaining existing legacy sort/order fields and explicit-sort shapes. Assurance risk was exercised against the declared recurrence policy to select existing gates; no thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-20T07:32:49.841Z","harness:codex","Full-run triage:10820 tests passed,7 assertions failed and3 platform skips. Updated the intended brief-row expectations and moved new tests below the unchanged120-file cap. Native continuation pages intentionally reference earlier metadata and end at next_cursor:null; acceptance now follows that advertised contract. The packed continuation suite passes unchanged after supplying Homebrew npm through NODE_PATH. A separate calibration gate drift is being diagnosed before closure. The simultaneous static command waited behind the full-run build lease and timed out; subsequent validation is serialized."
  "2026-10-20T07:37:14.876Z","harness:codex","Measured encoding review: switching effective comparator stages from repeated objects to named [field,order] tuples reduces policy JSON from233 to128 bytes. The full5-command session at2243 synthetic items drops9696 to9664 estimated tokens (38778 to38650 bytes), while priority plus complete ordering metadata changes the bounded seen-item set108 to107. All2243 rows remain required by complete list/search cursor walks. The2-item session rises3454 to3474 tokens (+73 bytes). Regenerating the approved semantic calibration through its official --update path records this intentional richer-context tradeoff; declared token budgets, gate assertions, full-population parity and exact coverage thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T07:52:49.721Z","harness:codex","The unchanged token-budget gate now passes all32 surfaces after compacting only JSON whitespace for brief list envelopes; every item field, envelope field and receipt survives. Focused formatter/SDK acceptance passes92tests, including generic JSON formatting compatibility and full JSON round-trip. Help and generated contracts now correctly describe the leading sort column. No token-budget ceiling was raised. Recorded additional SDK typing follow-up pm-oybmsd as open/unclaimed; the intentional sparse continuation runtime remains intact."
  "2026-10-20T08:05:52.616Z","harness:codex","Static validation caught an independent replay oracle that assumed all JSON used two-space indentation. Updated that oracle to infer compact versus pretty encoding from exact captured wire bytes, reject other encodings, and independently recompute receipt and normalized-comparison costs in the observed encoding. Existing forged-count/section/envelope controls now execute for both encodings; no producer formatter is imported into the oracle and no gate ceiling is changed."
  "2026-10-20T08:13:14.469Z","harness:codex","Token-budget review: kept the 32-surface hard token-budget ceilings unchanged. Compact brief JSON saves whitespace without dropping any semantic fields; accounting independently validates compact or pretty JSON and rejects other encodings. The deterministic agent-task replay now costs 13676 tokens across the unchanged transcript versus 13795 previously: the four-read orientation falls 2325 -> 2139 while triage rises 552 -> 619 because it now carries all four effective comparator stages. Approved baseline regeneration records that specific information tradeoff; transcript digest, required facts, orientation winner (1087), refusal comparisons, negative controls and per-step regression checks remain enforced."
